What Is It?
~~~~~~~~~~~
    Quips is my idea of those little sayings that pop up before the MAIN
prompt, although I've made mine so they pop up in front of ALL major prompts
throughout the bbs. Using the command "EQ" (Edit Quip), your users can edit
a quip to hold any text they wish. Using the "EQ x", where "x" is a number
from 1 to 100 will allow anyone to edit a specific Quip. This could allow
you to edit quips you notice may contain foul language or other material you
deem inadequate on your BBS. Quips can be up to 60 characters in length and
may contain any MCI codes the user has access to. SysOps could even create
Quips containing the MCI {* } command to display text file quips, etc. Each
Quip entered will be ENDED with the MCI \q1 command, if not already done to
insure the MCI's used don't run away on the rest of your system.

How Do I Install It?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1: Copy "Quips!", "QuipShow", and the "Quips/" directory into your PFILES:
   path. (If you wish to keep THIS file, toss it into the "Quips/" Dir)

2: Using LHA, unarc the contents of the "quips_data.lha" archive into the
   "pfiles:quips/" directory. There should be 100 files upon completion.
   (101 files, including the archive! hehe)

3: Now, load your "cnet:bbsmenu" file into a text editor and add the following
   line to the end of Menu # 2, Available Everywhere:

        EQ, Edit Quip       `1-       |   {#0 pfiles:Quips!}
                                          ^
4: You now need to add the following MCI Commands to the FRONT of one or
   more of the following lines in your "cnet:bbstext" file, depending on
   how often you wish the Quips to be displayed. As I stated earlier, I
   have them running at ALL of the following locations, so I KNOW for FACT
   they work in these locations.

                {T55 #3}{JE 2+}{#0pfiles:QuipShow}{2}
                ^       ^      ^                  ^
                `-------`------|------------------'
                           Control-Q's

   The {T55 #3} and {JE 2+} MCI commands test the user's HELP Level, and if
   it's set to "3" (SuperUser), then the Quip's will be SKIPPED. You can
   change the "3" to a "2" or whatever if you wish to lower the HELP Level
   used. Remember, there are FOUR(4) Control-Q's used in the above line!

   OK, so you take the ABOVE line and place it in FRONT of one or more of
   the following lines in BBSTEXT:

        CNet Prompt  Line#  What's on that line(In Stock 3.0 BBSTEXT File)
      =====================================================================
        Main Prompt   68:   \n1\q0\c6Main> \q1
        UDBase/Base  397:   \n1\q0\c6%s> \q1
        P-Files      672:   \n1\q0\c6Program files> \q1
        G-Files      673:   \n1\q0\c6General files> \q1
        News Files   674:   \n1\q0\c6News files> \q1
        Voting      1531:   \n1\q0\c6Voting (topic#, List, New, Quit)> \q1
        BBS-List    1610:   \n1\q0\c6BBSList> \q1

   And finally, here's what the lines should look like AFTER you've made the
   stated additions:

